1 REM ============================================================
2 REM  t61_print_using.bpp
3 REM  BASIC++ PRINT USING Test & Tutorial
4 REM ============================================================
5 REM
6 REM  PRINT USING formats output according to a format string.
7 REM  This is essential for creating formatted reports, aligning
8 REM  columns, and controlling decimal precision.
9 REM
10 REM  FORMAT CHARACTERS:
11 REM    # (hash)    - Digit position. Shows digit or space.
12 REM    . (dot)     - Decimal point position
13 REM    , (comma)   - Insert comma every 3 digits
14 REM    ** (stars)  - Fill leading spaces with asterisks
15 REM    $$ (dollar) - Floating dollar sign
16 REM    + (plus)    - Show sign (+ or -)
17 REM    - (minus)   - Trailing minus for negatives
18 REM    ^ (caret)   - Scientific notation
19 REM    ! (bang)    - First character of string
20 REM    \ \ (slashes) - Fixed-width string field
21 REM    & (amper)   - Entire string
22 REM
23 DIALECT "GWBS"
24 REM
100 REM === Numeric formatting ===
101 REM PRINT USING "format"; value
102 REM The format string controls how the value is displayed.
110 TEST "PRINT USING numeric"
120 PRINT USING "###.##"; 3.14
130 REM Output: "  3.14" (right-justified in 6 chars)
140 PRINT USING "###.##"; 99.9
150 REM Output: " 99.90" (trailing zero added)
160 PRINT USING "#####"; 42
170 REM Output: "   42" (padded with spaces)
180 ENDTEST
200 REM === String formatting ===
210 TEST "PRINT USING string"
220 PRINT USING "!"; "HELLO"
230 REM Output: "H" (first character only)
240 PRINT USING "&"; "HELLO"
250 REM Output: "HELLO" (entire string)
260 ENDTEST
300 REM === Multiple values ===
310 TEST "PRINT USING multiple"
320 PRINT USING "### ###"; 10; 20
330 REM Output: " 10  20"
340 ENDTEST
9999 END
